# Line endings for files the harness parses line by line or runs as scripts: always LF, whatever the checkout's core.autocrlf.
# In the app: nothing at runtime; git applies it on checkout and commit.
# Used by: git. Why each line is here, and nothing else is:
#   *.mdc, *.md — scripts/sync-claude-rules.mjs, plans-status.mjs, and human-checks.mjs match `---\n` / `\n` line shapes;
#                 a CRLF rule would read as a skill and drop out of AGENTS.md (the sync now also tolerates CRLF).
#   *.sh, .githooks/* — a CRLF shebang (`bash\r`) won't run, so a Windows checkout's pre-push would fail to start.
*.mdc text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
